From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] localspl, winprint: a job's whole JOB_INFO; a job a maker's print processor gives up on is printed by winprint

What Samsung's Universal Print Driver 3 needs:

- localspl: GetJob level 1 and 2 give the job's datatype, user, machine,
  priority and (level 2) print processor and notify name; they gave the
  document and printer names only. Samsung's driver renders a job only if
  its datatype is EMF (it read a NULL datatype and crashed). A job looked up
  that does not exist is ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.
- localspl: a maker's print processor that gives up on a job without opening
  its data at all: the job is printed by winprint through the driver
  instead of being lost. Samsung's processor (us006pc) does so here after
  reading the printer data value "EndDoc<job>"; whether the value is there
  or not makes no difference to it (tried with values 0-3), so what it
  waits for is not that value, and we do not take its code apart to find
  out.
- winprint: the job our 64-bit host holds for a 32-bit program's job (1032)
  is an EMF job, as the program's is, and is aborted, not printed.
- winprint: a page's frame is rounded to the nearest pixel below the origin
  too (it truncated toward zero), for 1041's frames around the printable
  origin.

Test: test/drvpkg-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_JOBINFO), test/printproc-gate.sh
(mutant SG_MUTANT_PPFALLBACK).
